# CLAUDE.md — global

Applies to every project on this machine. Project-level `CLAUDE.md` files
add to this; they do not replace it.

Keep this file under 200 lines. Past that it stops being read — by people
and by the model — and a rule nobody reads is worse than no rule, because
it reads as covered.

---

## This machine

Built from `wb-setup` (`__ROOT__`). Identity lives in `~/.sop-vars` and
nowhere else — `ORG`, `BRAND`, `GH_USER`, `GIT_EMAIL`, `OPERATOR_PHONE`,
`WORK_REPO`, `GRAPH_PACK`. Read from there rather than hardcoding a value
in a script; that habit is the whole reason this build is reproducible.

`MACHINE` and `TAILNET` are deliberately not variables. Resolve them from
Tailscale at runtime.

The full build procedure is `~/.claude/SOP.md`. `bash __ROOT__/verify.sh`
reports what is actually true right now, which is usually the fastest way
to answer "is X set up on this machine".

---

## Standing rules

**Never fabricate.** An unknown field stays empty and the absence
propagates honestly. A plausible guess costs more than a gap, because a
gap is visible and a wrong value is not.

**Say which class of verification you ran.** Executions (it exited 0),
eyeballs (a human looked), and assertions (a test failed before the fix
and passes after) are three different claims. Reach for assertions before
saying something is verified.

**Match the surrounding code.** Comment density, naming, and idiom are
part of the interface. New code that reads as foreign is a cost paid by
whoever touches it next.

**Report outcomes plainly.** If tests fail, say so with the output. If a
step was skipped, say that. When something is done and verified, say it
without hedging.

---

## Before committing

- Tests pass. A failing suite means the commit does not land.
- No secrets in source. Check the diff, not just intent.
- Commit as `$GH_USER`. A second identity blocks deploys and is painful
  to unwind after the fact.

---

## Delivery

Text goes to `$OPERATOR_PHONE` over iMessage. Text is reliable;
attachments are not — send one live link, never a `localhost` or
`.local` URL, and bind dev servers `-H 0.0.0.0` so the tailnet can
actually reach them.
